+# S7: the touches of TEST22 went to `SBAlertItemWindow`, not to a cover sheet
+
+TEST22B/E (`artifacts/vayu/test22-lead2-20261028`) had Preferences in the foreground but
+`inactive`, and every synthetic touch went to one SpringBoard context. The S6 run read that as a
+cover sheet and looked for `-dismissCoverSheetAnimated:completion:`, which does not exist in
+SpringBoard 16.5. The window stack that S6 0006 added answers it:
+
+```
+hakios: layers: 13 windows
+hakios: layers: window SBAlertItemWindow level 2000, context 0x5c18e2a6 (secure, ...)
+hakios: layers:   ... "VC:SBAlertItemRootViewController" ...
+hakios: layers:       ... "VC:_SBAlertController" ... 270x210.333
+hakios: layers:         _UILabelLayer ... 238x42.3333      (title)
+hakios: layers:         _UILabelLayer ... 238x95.6667      (body)
+hakios: layers:         ... _UIAlertControllerActionView ... 134.667x44
+hakios: layers:         ... _UIAlertControllerActionView ... 135x44
+```
+
+and backboardd:
+
+```
+[TouchEvents] touchstats ... destinations: {
+    SpringBoard.10 contextID 5C18E2A6: { touchIDs: 1-6; };
+}
+```
+
+`5C18E2A6` is exactly that window. There is no `SBCoverSheetWindow` in the stack at all.
+
+## What the alert is
+
+`SBActivationFailedAlertItem`, built by the telephony layer:
+
+- `-[SBTelephonyManager _provisioningUpdateWithStatus:slot:]` (`0x1c4b29ef4`) makes it with
+  `-initWithFailureCount:slot:`; the classref loaded at `0x1c4b2a0c0` (`0x1de7c9498`) is
+  `SBActivationFailedAlertItem`;
+- `-[SBTelephonyManager _setCurrentActivationAlertItem:]` (`0x1c4b29e50`) deactivates the old
+  item and calls `-[SBAlertItemsController activateAlertItem:]` for the new one.
+
+The fake SIM of `vayu_cell` never reports "activated", so the item is presented at boot and stays:
+the application's scene is foreground, but the modal alert makes SpringBoard's scene the active
+one, so the app is `inactive`, gets no touches and has nothing to redraw. That is the "1 frame a
+second" of TEST20B/S6.
+
+## The real cover-sheet API (for the record)
+
+- `-_dismissCoverSheetAnimated:withCompletion:` belongs to
+  `SBCoverSheetSlidingViewController` (`0x1c4a7e378`), not to the presentation manager.
+- `SBCoverSheetPresentationManager` (`+sharedInstance` `0x1c4a1300c`) has
+  `-setCoverSheetPresented:animated:withCompletion:` (`0x1c4a937f4`) and
+  `-setCoverSheetPresented:animated:options:withCompletion:` (`0x1c4a7e2c0`);
+  `-isPresented` is `0x1c4a39aec`.
+
+## What S7 does
+
+Boot-arg `s7=1`:
+
+1. replaces `-[SBTelephonyManager _setCurrentActivationAlertItem:]`; an item is logged and dropped
+   (the original is called with nil, which deactivates anything already up);
+2. `com.hakios.ready` dismisses an alert that was presented before the hook
+   (`SBAlertItemsController`: `visibleAlertItem`, `hasVisibleAlert`,
+   `canDeactivateAlertForMenuClickOrSystemGesture`,
+   `deactivateAlertItemsOfClass:reason:animated:`, `deactivateAlertItem:`,
+   `_clearAllQueuedAlertItems`), then the application switcher
+   (`SBMainSwitcherControllerCoordinator`: `isMainSwitcherVisible`/`isAnySwitcherVisible`,
+   `dismissMainSwitcherNoninteractivelyAnimated:NO`,
+   `dismissAllSwitchersNoninteractivelyAnimated:NO`), then the cover sheet if it is up
+   (`setCoverSheetPresented:NO animated:NO withCompletion:nil`);
+3. `com.hakios.activate` is the last resort: `SBUIController
+   activateApplication:fromIcon:nil location:0 activationSettings:nil actions:nil` for
+   `com.apple.Preferences` from `SBApplicationController`;
+4. the self-test (`s7=1`) posts `com.hakios.ready` before opening Settings and again after the
+   application is up; it probes a tap after each, and on failure posts ready+activate and probes
+   once more.
+
+The run without `s7=1` behaves exactly as before; `s6_coversheet=1` still works as the old path.
+
+## What to read in the next log
+
+- `hakios: s7=1: -[SBTelephonyManager _setCurrentActivationAlertItem:] replaced`
+- `hakios: alerts: ... hasVisibleAlert ...` / `dropped ... SBActivationFailedAlertItem`
+- `hakios: switcher: ...` / `hakios: coversheet: ...`
+- `hakios: layers: window SBAlertItemWindow ...` must be absent; touchstats must name
+  `Preferences.<pid> contextID ...`
+- `PROBE: the application got the tap ...`, `the application is active`, `S5: N events`,
+  `S5FPS ... 60+ frames (... a second)`.
